        ],
        "dateModified": "2022-12-13T11:07:29+00:00",
        "image": "https://www.enworld.org/attachments/cd43773e1ac7429021bb920577aaf0c5-2789645563-jpg.269549/",
        "text": "Kim Mohan, known for work at TSR and Wizards of the Coast, editor-in-chief of Dragon Magazine, author of the AD&D 1E Wilderness Survival Guide, and much more, passed away yesterday aged 73.\n\nKim joined TSR in 1979, and became editor-in-chief of Dragon Magazine in 1989. He joined Gary Gygax's New Infinity Productions in 1986, but later returned to D&D, working on D&D 3E at WotC. He retired in 2013.\n\nIndustry veterans have been paying tribute to Kim on social media and elsewhere."
    },
